WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:05.690
Three easy exercises that help with high blood pressure. You can do them at home.

00:06.190 --> 00:12.560
One. Brisk walking. Aim for thirty minutes, five days a week. Three ten-minute walks count too.

00:13.060 --> 00:21.910
Two. Sit to stand. Stand up from a firm chair without using your hands, then sit back down slowly. Do it ten times, twice a day.

00:22.410 --> 00:30.490
Three. Wall push-ups. Stand an arm's length from a wall, put your hands on it, bend your elbows, then push back. Ten times.

00:30.990 --> 00:37.640
Keep breathing all the way through. Holding your breath can make your blood pressure spike. Breathe out as you push.

00:38.140 --> 00:48.440
Stop if you feel chest pain, dizziness, or very short of breath, and tell your doctor. If your BP is very high, check with them before you start.
